# The PRE-LANE WHOLE-DESKTOP BASELINE of smoke-1x-D.env: the same advertisement, the same legs, the
# same windows and the same (unchecked) display -- only the RAIL work area differs. Since F-ja-4
# lane E the bridge sends the primary display's visibleFrame as the server's work area after every
# start command, and smoke-1x-D.env (which does not mention WORK_AREA) measures exactly that. This
# job turns it off, so the server keeps the start command's own whole-desktop work area, which is
# what every run before the lane measured.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS (lane E gate r1, section 4 (f), observation): the first batch after the merge runs
# the work area by default, and a comparison against the older recordings needs each form run once
# in the same shape -- the default and this one -- to confirm that the move / resize legs judged at
# tolerance 0 do not depend on the whole-desktop work area. Expected readings, from the in-session
# sampler's `wa=` field:
#   this job (work area off)        the whole desktop, wa=0,0,<desktop w>,<desktop h> -- on the
#                                   lab's QHD panel wa=0,0,2560,1440, the 2026-09-21 baseline
#   smoke-1x-D.env (the default)    wa=0,30,2560,1350 (in person, 2026-10-22)
#
# Consumed by smoke-job.command (via `run-scenario.sh smoke 1x-D-wa0`), never by relay.command: it
# carries no PROGRAM and opens no redirected drive. Run it into the same dated evidence directory as
# its default sibling by naming the batch on the command line:
#     Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh smoke 1x-D     <dated batch>
#     Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh smoke 1x-D-wa0 <dated batch>
# The tracked BATCH below is the lane name, not a date.
TAG=1xD-wa0
BATCH=fja4-work-area

# PREFLIGHT 1 (the display): deliberately EMPTY, for the reason smoke-1x-D.env gives -- the ordinary
# 1x display is not one looks-like string, so the check is never asked and the evidence states the
# display instead.
DISPLAY_LOOKS_LIKE=

# Identical to the sibling: the product default advertisement (the knob left unset).
ADVERTISED_SCALE=D

# The scenario legs, identical to the sibling, so the move / resize legs are the thing compared.
MOVE=1
MAXIMIZE=0
TRAY=0
TRAY_CLICK=0
EXTRA_APPS=notepad
MOVE_TARGET='Notepad|记事本'

# THE ONE DIFFERENCE. 0 puts WINDOW_SMOKE_WORK_AREA=0 in the child, which forces the work area off:
# all four work-area properties stay 0, the bridge sends nothing, and the server keeps the start
# command's whole-desktop work area. (The key's direction is the opposite of EDGE_PROFILE's and
# MOVE_KEEP's: 1, or the key absent, leaves the knob unset = the product work area.)
WORK_AREA=0

# PREFLIGHT 2 (the checkout). The knob this run is named for must exist in the tree about to be
# built: a checkout that predates lane E has no work-area knob and no work-area send, so it would
# run the pre-lane wire anyway and nothing in its evidence would say why.
REQUIRE_SYMBOL=WINDOW_SMOKE_WORK_AREA
